COMIC PRODUCTION RULES
1. Dialogue-first composition: Finalize the dialogue for every panel before generating artwork. Place provisional speech bubbles in the storyboard, then position characters and faces around them.
2. Character consistency: Use the established character reference images, not new interpretations of Dr. Ananya, Meera, Ravi and the supporting cast.
3. Branding: Page 1: no Welbuk name, icon or branded screens. Pages 2-24: official hot-pink and white Welbuk identity. Brand pink: #FF0066. Do not generate alternative blue, teal, heart-shaped or medical-cross Welbuk logos. Apply the authentic supplied logos during final composition.
4. Speech balloons: All dialogue belongs inside its respective panel, not below the page. Reserve sufficient room for bubble lettering. Bubble tails must point to the correct speaker. No important face, hand, clinical action or UI element should be hidden.
5. Visual storytelling: Use varied shot distances and meaningful transitions. Avoid repeated character portraits, repetitive identical panel grids and overly long explanatory bubbles.
6. Interface accuracy: Use real product UI references when available. Illustrative screenshots must not be mistaken for literal production screens. Use fictional patient data.
7. Product-status accuracy: Do not present staging functionality, work-in-progress infrastructure, or future network features as already released.
8. Medical responsibility: Doctors remain responsible for diagnosis, prescribing, triage, and clinical decisions. AI-assisted documentation requires appropriate consent and clinician review.
9. Quality review: Before accepting each page, verify: correct page number and story sequence; natural left-to-right reading order; clear panel-to-panel continuity; correct dialogue and spelling; speech bubbles connected to the right characters; no covered faces, hands or important objects; consistent characters and official branding; appropriate product-status labels; no unsupported clinical or commercial claims.
10. Final deliverables: Individual high-resolution pages 01-24; one combined 24-page comic PDF; mobile-friendly reading edition; editable dialogue and page-layout source; character/reference and generation manifests.

